From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: marty <marty@fyai.co.nz>
Date: Tue, 9 Sep 2026 19:30:00 +1200
Subject: [PATCH] Only reopen the stream when the geometry changes

SET_GEOMETRY is defined as a cheap, cosmetic update, so cores are free to
send it every frame and some do: yabasanshiro re-announces 704x448 on each
retro_run. Closing the stream unconditionally turned that into a reopen per
frame, and every reopen sets CRPRenderManager's flush flag, so the render
thread destroyed and rebuilt the whole buffer pool at frame rate.

Panzer Dragoon II ran ~6000 of those cycles in 107 seconds before the render
thread destroyed a buffer the game loop was still holding and Kodi took a
SIGBUS in CBaseRenderBufferPool::Flush(), branching to 0x61.

Comparing first costs nothing and leaves a genuine resolution change - which
is what the reopen is for - working as before.
---
diff --git a/src/video/VideoGeometry.h b/src/video/VideoGeometry.h
--- a/src/video/VideoGeometry.h
+++ b/src/video/VideoGeometry.h
@@ -20,6 +20,15 @@ namespace LIBRETRO
     CVideoGeometry(CVideoGeometry&) = default;
     CVideoGeometry(const retro_game_geometry &geometry);
 
+    bool operator==(const CVideoGeometry &rhs) const
+    {
+      return m_nominalWidth == rhs.m_nominalWidth &&
+             m_nominalHeight == rhs.m_nominalHeight &&
+             m_maxWidth == rhs.m_maxWidth &&
+             m_maxHeight == rhs.m_maxHeight &&
+             m_displayAspectRatio == rhs.m_displayAspectRatio;
+    }
+
     void UpdateVideoGeometry(const retro_game_geometry &geometry);
 
     unsigned int NominalWidth() const { return m_nominalWidth; }
diff --git a/src/video/VideoStream.cpp b/src/video/VideoStream.cpp
--- a/src/video/VideoStream.cpp
+++ b/src/video/VideoStream.cpp
@@ -36,8 +36,15 @@ void CVideoStream::Deinitialize()
 
 void CVideoStream::SetGeometry(const CVideoGeometry &geometry)
 {
+  // SET_GEOMETRY is cheap by contract, so cores send it whenever they feel
+  // like it - yabasanshiro sends the same 704x448 every frame. Reopening the
+  // stream for that flushes Kodi's render buffer pool at frame rate, and the
+  // render thread eventually frees a buffer the game loop still holds.
+  if (*m_geometry == geometry)
+    return;
+
   // Close stream so it can be reopened with the updated geometry
   if (m_addon != nullptr)
     CloseStream();
 
   *m_geometry = geometry;
 }
